      "category": "answerable",
      "question": "Which optimizer and beta values were used to train the Transformer, and how many learning-rate warmup steps were used?",
      "expected_behavior": "answer",
      "relevant_paper": "arXiv:1706.03762v7",
      "note": null,
      "status": "answered",
      "answer": "The Transformer was trained with the Adam optimizer, using β1 = 0.9 and β2 = 0.98, and the learning‑rate schedule employed 4000 warmup steps. [S1]",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The Transformer was trained with the Adam optimizer, using β1 = 0.9 and β2 = 0.98, and the learning‑rate schedule employed 4000 warmup steps.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "source_id": "S1",
              "paper_title": "Attention Is All You Need",
              "arxiv_id": "1706.03762",
              "version": 7,
              "pages": [
                7
              ],
              "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.03762v7#page=7",
              "chunk_id": "10756f19bc1d360711b8f7e74b4c5ec9ae55fec784d217f073162c7d4b57bbf4",
              "char_start": 21093,
              "quote": "We used the Adam optimizer [20] with β1 = 0.9, β2 = 0.98 and ε = 10^{−9}. We varied the learning\nrate over the course of training, according to the formula:\n\nlrate = d^{−0.5}\n\nmodel ^{·min(step_num−0.5, step_num·warmup_steps−1.5)}\n(3)\n\nThis corresponds to increasing the learning rate linearly for the first warmup_steps training steps,\nand decreasing it thereafter proportionally to the inverse square root of the step number. We used\nwarmup_steps = 4000."
            }
          ]
        }
